{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trip record carries a DRIVER 'arrived' event at 2026-09-10T06:50:20 on EV-TRIP-09110, and the driver's GPS trace on EV-GPS-09110 sits a mean distance of 24.0 m from the pickup pin — far inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — with the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 06:50:00, twenty seconds BEFORE the arrival event. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are both satisfied and the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09110", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver held a single continuous in-geofence position for 330 seconds (first fix 06:50:00, last fix 06:55:30, 34 consecutive qualifying fixes at 0.0 kph), which exceeds the 300-second STANDARD minimum dwell by 30 seconds. POL-NS-01 limb (c) is satisfied, and the dwell is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix as the clause requires, not from the 'arrived' tap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip was terminated by the DRIVER at 06:55:30 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW — at or after the moment the required 300-second dwell elapsed at 06:55:00 — and the record shows no boarding event, so POL-NS-01 limb (d) is satisfied on one of the three recognised reason codes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancelled_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 cannot rescue the rider: the wrong-entrance route applies only where the driver is stationary OUTSIDE the POL-NS-02 arrival radius (while within 400 m). Here every one of the 34 qualifying driver fixes is about 24 m from the pin, inside the 50 m radius, so there was no mislocation of any kind and the clause has no field to operate on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.driver_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider. Limb (b) fails because the driver answered the rider's 06:51:40 'Coming down now.' with 'Okay, waiting.' at 06:52:00 — twenty seconds later, well inside the 120-second window, and no in-app call was needed. Limb (c) also fails independently: the rider's own track places her 519.4 m from the pin with zero qualifying fixes inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09110", "EV-GPS-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no false arrival marker under POL-NS-05. Matched to the 'arrived' timestamp, the GPS places the driver about 24 m from the pin — far below the 300 m threshold — and travelling at 0.0 kph, below the 15 kph motion threshold. The waiting clock was properly started and the arrival marker is genuine, not the early-tap the clause punishes.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-06 does not apply because there is no shortfall to excuse: the effective in-geofence dwell is 330 seconds against a 300-second minimum, a surplus of 30 seconds. I note for completeness that the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0) and is NOT relied upon by this claim; its absence serves only to close the limb (i) accumulation route, which this single uninterrupted 330-second run does not need.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09110", "EV-ADVIS-09110-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.accumulated_sec"
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat record is clean and shows the driver doing exactly what the framework asks: a SYSTEM 'Your driver has arrived' at 06:50:21, the driver's own locating message 'At Block 612 lobby pickup.' at 06:50:35, and a further reply 'Okay, waiting.' at 06:52:00, with no messaging gap over the waiting window and a message count (4) that reconciles with trip_record.chat_message_count — so there is no POL-NS-08(c) chat defect.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.chat_message_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line is internally sound. Under the fee_schedule resolution_rule the chargeable fee is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), which is SGD 4.00 and matches the fare_breakdown line exactly, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare-integrity defect and no integrity route to a refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fee_charged",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own trace confirms she was never at the pickup point: all 16 of her fixes sit 519.4 m from the pin and not one falls inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. This is a genuine no-show, not a driver-side coordination failure, and it corroborates the driver's RIDER_NO_SHOW termination.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "With POL-NS-01 satisfied in full and nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's compensation at 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee — SGD 3.20 — the residual 20 percent being the platform service fee. The disposition of the fee itself is NO_ACTION, so the rider's challenge fails and the charge stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09110", "EV-TRIP-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-NS-07 anti-farming bar is not met and compensation must not be withheld: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the absolute threshold of 4, and 1 divided by completed_trips_30d of 120 is 0.008, below the 0.08 rate threshold. Both limbs are required and neither is met, so the check does not trip and no escalation follows from it. I rely on the two citable counters only, not on the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "To the extent the Judge examines the POL-NS-09(c) repeat-dispute trigger on the two counterparty counters (rider and driver each record disputes_with_counterparty_90d = 2, and the rider's own filing calls this 'another dispute with the same driver'), any escalation there is terminal and, per POL-GEN-03, HOLDS the SGD 4.00 fee rather than refunding it. On no reading that this record supports does the driver lose the charge, and the reviewer should be told that the fee is chargeable on the merits set out above.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09110", "EV-DPROF-09110"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the underlying arithmetic, and so do I. The driver's arrival marker at 06:50:20 is corroborated by the GPS trace: the first in-geofence fix at 06:50:00 sits about 24 m from the pickup pin, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (POL-NS-02), and the trace shows a single unbroken in-geofence hold of 330 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum (POL-NS-01(c)), with the trip ended by the driver at 06:55:30 under RIDER_NO_SHOW after that dwell elapsed and no boarding event (POL-NS-01(d)). The rider's own track places her 519.4 m from the pin throughout and the driver replied to her message within 120 seconds, so POL-NS-04 does not apply, and POL-NS-03, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 do not apply either. On the merits the SGD 4.00 fee is chargeable, the anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination against 120 completed trips in 30 days, below both the count of 4 and the rate of 0.08), and absent anything else the driver would be owed SGD 3.20 (80% of SGD 4.00) under POL-NS-07.\n\nThis case cannot be decided here. POL-NS-09(c) requires escalation where rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d together show 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. Both counters read 2, and the rider's own filing describes this as 'another dispute with the same driver.' The trigger is met, and escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal: it replaces any monetary outcome, so no refund and no compensation issue. The SGD 4.00 sits at payment_status PENDING and is HELD — not collected from the rider, not refunded to her — until a human reviewer resolves it.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer is the repeat pattern between this rider and this driver: whether the earlier disputes in the 90-day window concern the same conduct, and whether the SGD 4.00 no-show fee should stand or be refunded in light of that history.\n\nTwo items do not change the outcome. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09110-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0); the rider cited it only for its absence, which closes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route but decides nothing, since the single 330-second hold already meets the minimum. The rest of the bundle is clean under POL-NS-08: no clock skew (20 s), no trace gap (34 fixes, 0 s maximum gap, rider_track present), the chat log reconciles (4 messages against chat_message_count 4), and the SGD 4.00 line matches the fee_schedule resolution rule (the greater of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee). The driver's anti-farming argument rests only on the citable counters no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d; the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only and was properly not used."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

