    "explanation": "To the Rider and the Driver: this ruling does not decide who keeps the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee. The case goes to a human reviewer with the fee held, because POL-NS-09(c) is engaged.\n\nOn the merits the fee is chargeable. The driver's 'arrived' event is at 06:50:20 and the GPS trace shows the first qualifying in-geofence fix at 06:50:00, twenty seconds earlier, about 24.0 m from the pin — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b), POL-NS-02). The driver then held position for one continuous 330-second run (06:50:00 to 06:55:30, 34 fixes at 0.0 kph), 30 seconds over the 300-second STANDARD minimum (POL-NS-01(c)), and the trip was terminated by the driver at 06:55:30 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed and with no boarding event recorded (POL-NS-01(d)). Nothing displaces the charge: there is no shortfall (POL-NS-06), the arrival marker was genuine — 24 m from the pin and 0.0 kph, far from the 300 m and 15 kph thresholds (POL-NS-05) — the rider sat 519.4 m from the pin with no qualifying fix inside the 100 m presence radius, and the driver answered her 06:51:40 message 20 seconds later, so POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her; POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance route does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it. The chat log is complete (4 messages, matching trip_record.chat_message_count) and the SGD 4.00 fee reconciles with the fee_schedule (the greater of the SGD 4.00 STANDARD zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee), so there is no POL-NS-08(c) or (d) defect.\n\nWhy the case still escalates: rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 2, and the rider's own filing describes this as 'another dispute with the same driver' — 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days, which POL-NS-09(c) makes a mandatory escalation. Only the two citable counterparty counters support this; the lifetime counters rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags (1) and driver_profile.prior_no_show_flags (2) are CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01 and form no part of the trigger. POL-NS-09 escalation is TERMINAL and replaces any monetary ruling, so I make no order on the rider's refund and none on the driver's compensation, which would otherwise have been SGD 3.20 — 80 percent of SGD 4.00 under POL-NS-07, the anti-farming check having not tripped (1 termination against a threshold of 4, and 1/120 = 0.008 against a rate threshold of 0.08, so both limbs fail and no instruction goes into the packet). The SGD 4.00 fee stays at payment_status PENDING and is held, neither collected nor refunded, while review is pending.\n\nNo referral fires. POL-NS-05(ii) is not engaged (the arrival marker was genuine, not false), and POL-NS-07's packet instruction applies only where its anti-farming branch trips, which it does not.\n\nThe open question for the reviewer, which belongs here rather than in a referral: whether the pattern of repeat no-show disputes between this same rider and driver indicates abuse on either side, which a single case file cannot fairly assess. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09110-01 (weight 0.0) is relied on for no positive fact; its absence only closes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route, which the single uninterrupted 330-second run does not need."
